loom 0.7.2 with one change to its DPOR (verus/loom/run.sh applies this to
a copy of the crate; `git apply -p1` in its root).

Stock loom races an atomic store or read-modify-write only against the
atomic's last access (`last_access`). When that access is a load that
happens before the store (usually the storing thread's own), an earlier
load by another thread is never raced, so the store is never run ahead
of it: a model whose defect needs that order passes, after as few as one
execution (`src/loom_tests/dpor.rs`). With this change a store or rmw
is also raced against each thread's last load of the atomic
(`last_loads`). The change only adds backtracking points: the DPOR
clocks (`dpor_vv`) are computed as in stock loom, so every schedule
stock loom explores is still explored. The same defect, found
independently, is fixed in ToyOSOrg/loom's `toyos` branch
(ToyOSOrg/ToyOS PR #567), which also joins those loads into the
storing thread's clock; that prunes more and is not done here.

